## 2. Send the report back — Write tool, then Bash, background

Write `$SCRATCH/msg-rdp-lang-report.txt`:

```
Reply in English. Ignore any pre-filled text in your input box.

rdp-lang — your DONE report at 4ba90e0 is REJECTED as delivered. It lists claims; the
brief's REPORT line requires skills used + their artifacts, and evidence as command output.

Do not edit, commit, amend, rebase or push: the head stays 4ba90e0. Touch no host.

Reply in the REPORT shape with:
1. superpowers:writing-plans — the plan file path and the commit that holds it.
2. superpowers:test-driven-development — the failing-test-first output (the red run,
   before the implementation) and `git log --oneline origin/main..4ba90e0`.
3. superpowers:verification-before-completion — the exact commands you ran at 4ba90e0
   and their raw output: each of the 23 tests by name and result, and ansible-lint.
4. "Idempotent re-run: changed=0" — the exact command, its target and its raw output.
   You have no host access in this project. If no such run took place, withdraw the
   line and say so.
5. Files changed (stat), docs touched, risks, open questions.

For any required skill you did not invoke, write "NOT USED". Do not reconstruct an
artifact after the fact: a phase that skipped its skill is redone with the skill.
"Ready to merge" is not yours to state.
```

```bash
herdr agent prompt rdp-lang "$(cat "$SCRATCH/msg-rdp-lang-report.txt")" --wait --timeout 600000; \
herdr agent read rdp-lang --source recent-unwrapped --lines 200 > "$ORCH_INBOX/rdp-lang.last"
```

## 3. My own run at the SHA — Bash, background

```bash
cd ~/work/ccs.ansible && git worktree add --detach .claude/worktrees/rdp-lang-verify 4ba90e0 && \
cd .claude/worktrees/rdp-lang-verify/projects/ccs && \
bash -c 'rc=0; ansible-lint || rc=1
  ansible-playbook --syntax-check playbooks/50-vm-app.yml || rc=1
  for t in tests/*.sh; do echo "== $t"; bash "$t" || { echo "FAIL $t"; rc=1; }; done
  echo "EXIT $rc"' </dev/null > "$SCRATCH/verify-rdp-lang-4ba90e0.log" 2>&1
```

